### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### Phase 5 — Subscriptions & Scheduled Orders Test Suite
### Sovva Backend (.NET 8)
###
### PREREQUISITES:
###   - User registered with primary address set (phase2)
###   - Wallet has sufficient balance (phase4 top-up)
###   - At least 1 meal + ingredients in DB
###
### FLOW (execute in order):
###   A. Create subscription → verify → deactivate → activate → delete
###   B. Duplicate prevention (same mealId → 409)
###   C. Admin manual processing
###   D. Scheduled order modification
###
### ENUM: SubscriptionFrequency
###   Daily=1, Alternate=2, Weekly=7, Monthly=30
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5257
@token = eyJhbGciOiJFUzI1NiIsImtpZCI6IjE4OTNiMDM2LWYyMTAtNDM4Ni1hNWJkLTk5ODA3N2FhOWYwNyIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..WGeKXQVoqbHwBu5wJtUdQ4Ap2EnuKsmQlly4c7uxYgzqk1y1NTWpZva49lnHvr3KVG_QkU8qyX0xKQxRjFtc6A

# Set from response values
@subscriptionId = 1
@scheduledOrderId = 1
@mealId = 1
@ingredientId1 = 1
@ingredientId2 = 2


### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### SCENARIO A — Create, Verify, Lifecycle
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### ─── A.1 POST create subscription — Daily ───────────────────────
### Expected: 201 Created → SubscriptionDto
### DTO: CreateSubscriptionDto {
###   mealId (required), frequency (required, enum int),
###   startDate (required, DateOnly), endDate (required, DateOnly),
###   active (default true), weeklySchedule? (for Weekly frequency)
### }
###
### IMPORTANT: startDate must be today or future
### endDate must be after startDate
### Service auto-creates first scheduled order for tomorrow

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Subscriptions HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "mealId": {{mealId}},
    "frequency": 1,
    "startDate": "2026-04-23",
    "endDate": "2026-05-23",
    "active": true
}

### SAVE: subscriptionId from response
###
### DB CHECK: SELECT * FROM subscriptions WHERE subscription_id = <id>
###   → active = true, frequency = 'Daily', meal_id = <mealId>
### DB CHECK: SELECT * FROM scheduled_orders WHERE subscription_id = <id>
###   → scheduled_for = tomorrow, order_status = 'Scheduled'
###   → has ingredients snapshot from the meal

###

### ─── A.2 GET active subscriptions — verify appears ──────────────
### Expected: 200 OK → array containing the subscription we just created
### Verify: subscriptionId from A.1 is in the list, active=true

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Subscriptions/active HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### ─── A.3 GET subscription by ID — verify details ────────────────
### Expected: 200 OK → SubscriptionDto with mealId + mealName
### Verify: mealId matches, frequency matches

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Subscriptions/{{subscriptionId}} HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### ─── A.4 GET all subscriptions ──────────────────────────────────
### Expected: 200 OK → array of all user's subscriptions

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Subscriptions HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### ─── A.5 GET my subscriptions ───────────────────────────────────
### Expected: 200 OK → same as above (user/me endpoint)

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Subscriptions/user/me HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### ─── A.6 PATCH deactivate subscription ──────────────────────────
### Expected: 200 OK → { message: "Subscription paused and order cancelled" }
###
### Side effects:
###   1. Subscription.IsActive = false
###   2. Tomorrow's scheduled_order status → Cancelled
###   3. SubscriptionSchedulingService.CancelOrderForSubscriptionAsync called

PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/Subscriptions/{{subscriptionId}}/deactivate HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### DB CHECK: SELECT active FROM subscriptions WHERE subscription_id = <id>
###   → active = false
### DB CHECK: SELECT order_status FROM scheduled_orders
###           WHERE subscription_id = <id> AND scheduled_for = tomorrow
###   → order_status = 'Cancelled'

###

### ─── A.7 GET active — subscription should NOT appear ────────────
### Expected: 200 OK → empty array (or without our subscription)

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Subscriptions/active HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### ─── A.8 PATCH activate subscription ────────────────────────────
### Expected: 200 OK → { message: "Subscription activated and order generated" }
###
### Side effects:
###   1. Subscription.IsActive = true
###   2. Tomorrow's scheduled_order recreated (status = Scheduled)

PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/Subscriptions/{{subscriptionId}}/activate HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### DB CHECK: SELECT active FROM subscriptions WHERE subscription_id = <id>
###   → active = true
### DB CHECK: SELECT * FROM scheduled_orders
###           WHERE subscription_id = <id> AND scheduled_for = tomorrow
###   → order_status = 'Scheduled' (new row created)

###

### ─── A.9 GET active — subscription should appear again ──────────
### Expected: 200 OK → array containing our subscription

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Subscriptions/active HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### ─── A.10 PUT update subscription ───────────────────────────────
### Expected: 200 OK → updated SubscriptionDto

PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/Subscriptions/{{subscriptionId}} HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "endDate": "2026-06-23",
    "active": true
}

###

### ─── A.11 DELETE subscription ───────────────────────────────────
### Expected: 204 No Content
###
### Side effects (DeleteSubscriptionAsync):
###   - Deletes subscription row
###   - Deletes pending scheduled_orders (isProcessedToOrder = false)
###   - Keeps processed orders (isProcessedToOrder = true) for history

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/Subscriptions/{{subscriptionId}} HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### DB CHECK: SELECT * FROM subscriptions WHERE subscription_id = <id>
###   → row deleted (or not found)
### DB CHECK: SELECT * FROM scheduled_orders WHERE subscription_id = <id>
###   → pending orders deleted
###   → processed orders (is_processed_to_order = true) still exist

###

### ─── A.12 GET subscription after delete — not found ─────────────
### Expected: 404 Not Found

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Subscriptions/{{subscriptionId}} HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### ─── A.13 DELETE subscription — already deleted ─────────────────
### Expected: 404 Not Found

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/Subscriptions/99999 HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###


