### SCENARIO B — Duplicate Prevention
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### ─── B.1 POST create subscription — first (setup) ───────────────
### Expected: 201 Created

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Subscriptions HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "mealId": {{mealId}},
    "frequency": 1,
    "startDate": "2026-04-23",
    "endDate": "2026-05-23"
}

### SAVE: subscriptionId for cleanup

###

### ─── B.2 POST create subscription — same mealId → 409 ──────────
### Expected: 409 Conflict → { error: "..." }
### SubscriptionService.CreateSubscriptionAsync checks
### GetAnyActiveSubscriptionByMealIdAsync before creating

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Subscriptions HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "mealId": {{mealId}},
    "frequency": 1,
    "startDate": "2026-04-23",
    "endDate": "2026-05-23"
}

###

### ─── B.3 Cleanup — delete the test subscription ─────────────────
### Expected: 204 No Content

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/Subscriptions/{{subscriptionId}} HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###


### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### SCENARIO B2 — Auth & Ownership Tests
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### ─── B2.1 POST create subscription — no auth ────────────────────
### Expected: 401 Unauthorized

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Subscriptions HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "mealId": {{mealId}},
    "frequency": 1,
    "startDate": "2026-04-23",
    "endDate": "2026-05-23"
}

###

### ─── B2.2 POST create subscription — invalid frequency ──────────
### Expected: 400 → { error: "..." } (ArgumentException from validator)

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Subscriptions HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "mealId": {{mealId}},
    "frequency": 999,
    "startDate": "2026-04-23",
    "endDate": "2026-05-23"
}

###

### ─── B2.3 POST create subscription — endDate before startDate ───
### Expected: 400 → { error: "..." }

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Subscriptions HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "mealId": {{mealId}},
    "frequency": 1,
    "startDate": "2026-05-23",
    "endDate": "2026-04-23"
}

###

### ─── B2.4 GET subscription — other user's subscription → 403 ────
### Expected: 403 Forbidden (ownership check: subscription.UserId != userId)

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Subscriptions/99999 HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### ─── B2.5 PATCH activate — other user's subscription → 403 ──────
### Expected: 403 Forbidden

PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/Subscriptions/99999/activate HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### ─── B2.6 PATCH deactivate — other user's subscription → 403 ────
### Expected: 403 Forbidden

PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/Subscriptions/99999/deactivate HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###


### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### SCENARIO C — Admin Manual Processing
### Controller: ScheduledOrdersController
### Base route: /api/ScheduledOrders
###
### IMPORTANT: Process endpoints convert scheduled_orders → orders:
###   1. Finds all Scheduled orders for target date
###   2. For each: deducts wallet → creates Order → marks processed
###   3. Returns ProcessOrdersResponseDto with counts
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### ─── C.0 Setup — create subscription so there's an order to process
### Expected: 201 Created → save subscriptionId

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Subscriptions HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "mealId": {{mealId}},
    "frequency": 1,
    "startDate": "2026-04-22",
    "endDate": "2026-05-22"
}

### SAVE: subscriptionId

###

### ─── C.1 POST process-today-manual (admin) ──────────────────────
### Expected: 200 OK → ProcessOrdersResponseDto {
###   processedDate, totalScheduled, successfullyProcessed,
###   alreadyProcessed, failed, results[]
### }

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ScheduledOrders/process-today-manual HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### DB CHECK: SELECT * FROM scheduled_orders
###           WHERE scheduled_for = today AND is_processed_to_order = true
###   → order_status = 'Confirmed'
### DB CHECK: SELECT * FROM orders WHERE scheduled_order_id IS NOT NULL
###   → new confirmed order row exists
### DB CHECK: SELECT * FROM wallet_transactions
###           WHERE description LIKE 'Order #%'
###   → exactly ONE debit per scheduled order (idempotency)
### DB CHECK: wallet_balance = previous - totalPrice (debited once only)

###

### ─── C.2 POST process-today-manual — idempotent ─────────────────
### Run again — should NOT double-charge
### Expected: 200 OK → alreadyProcessed count = previous successfullyProcessed
### No new wallet transactions created

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ScheduledOrders/process-today-manual HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### DB CHECK: wallet_balance unchanged from C.1
### DB CHECK: No new wallet_transactions rows

###

### ─── C.3 POST process-yesterday-manual (admin) ──────────────────
### Expected: 200 OK → ProcessOrdersResponseDto (may have 0 scheduled)

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ScheduledOrders/process-yesterday-manual HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### ─── C.4 POST process-tomorrow-manual (admin) ───────────────────
### Expected: 200 OK → ProcessOrdersResponseDto

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ScheduledOrders/process-tomorrow-manual HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### ─── C.5 POST process-today — no auth ───────────────────────────
### Expected: 401 Unauthorized

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ScheduledOrders/process-today-manual HTTP/1.1

###

### ─── C.6 Cleanup — delete test subscription ─────────────────────

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/Subscriptions/{{subscriptionId}} HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###


### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### SCENARIO D — Scheduled Order Cart Modification
### Controller: ScheduledOrdersController
###
### FLOW:
###   1. Create a subscription (generates tomorrow's order)
###   2. View tomorrow's cart
###   3. Modify ingredients
###   4. Cancel the order
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### ─── D.0 Setup — create subscription for cart testing ────────────

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Subscriptions HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "mealId": {{mealId}},
    "frequency": 1,
    "startDate": "2026-04-23",
    "endDate": "2026-05-23"
}

### SAVE: subscriptionId from response

###

### ─── D.1 GET tomorrow's scheduled orders ────────────────────────
### Expected: 200 OK → array of ScheduledOrderResponseDto
### Only shows orders with status = "Scheduled" (filtered by controller)
### SAVE: scheduledOrderId from first item

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/ScheduledOrders/tomorrow HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### ─── D.2 GET tomorrow — no auth ─────────────────────────────────
### Expected: 401 Unauthorized

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/ScheduledOrders/tomorrow HTTP/1.1

###

### ─── D.3 PUT modify scheduled order — change ingredients ────────
### Expected: 200 OK → { message: "Scheduled order modified successfully" }
###
### DTO: ModifyScheduledOrderDto {
###   selectedIngredients: [{ ingredientId, quantity }],
###   deliveryTimeSlot?, nutritionalSummary?
### }

PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/ScheduledOrders/{{scheduledOrderId}}/modify HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "selectedIngredients": [
        { "ingredientId": {{ingredientId1}}, "quantity": 2 },
        { "ingredientId": {{ingredientId2}}, "quantity": 3 }
    ],
    "deliveryTimeSlot": "9:00 AM"
}

### DB CHECK: SELECT * FROM scheduled_order_ingredients
###           WHERE scheduled_order_id = <id>
###   → quantities updated to 2 and 3
### DB CHECK: SELECT delivery_time_slot FROM scheduled_orders WHERE id = <id>
###   → "9:00 AM"

###

### ─── D.4 PUT modify — not found ─────────────────────────────────
### Expected: 400 → { error: "..." } (InvalidOperationException)

PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/ScheduledOrders/99999/modify HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "selectedIngredients": [
        { "ingredientId": {{ingredientId1}}, "quantity": 1 }
    ]
}

###

### ─── D.5 POST duplicate scheduled order ─────────────────────────
### Expected: 200 OK → ScheduledOrderResponseDto (new order for tomorrow)

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ScheduledOrders/{{scheduledOrderId}}/duplicate HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### ─── D.6 DELETE cancel scheduled order ──────────────────────────
### Expected: 200 OK → { message: "Scheduled order cancelled successfully" }
### NOTE: Only works for Scheduled status, not already processed

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/ScheduledOrders/{{scheduledOrderId}}/cancel HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### DB CHECK: SELECT order_status FROM scheduled_orders WHERE id = <id>
###   → 'Cancelled'

###

### ─── D.7 DELETE cancel — already cancelled ──────────────────────
### Expected: 400 → { error: "..." } (InvalidOperationException)

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/ScheduledOrders/{{scheduledOrderId}}/cancel HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### ─── D.8 DELETE cancel — not found ──────────────────────────────
### Expected: 400 → { error: "..." }

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/ScheduledOrders/99999/cancel HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### ─── D.9 POST create from meal builder (direct) ─────────────────
### Creates a standalone scheduled order (not from subscription)
### Expected: 200 OK → ScheduledOrderResponseDto
###
### DTO: CreateScheduledOrderDto {
###   mealName?, mealId?, mealImageUrl?, mealPrice?,
###   selectedIngredients[{ ingredientId, quantity }],
###   scheduledFor (DateTimeOffset), deliveryTimeSlot,
###   deliveryAddressId?, nutritionalSummary?, subscriptionId?
### }

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ScheduledOrders/create-from-meal-builder HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "mealName": "Test Standalone Order",
    "mealId": {{mealId}},
    "selectedIngredients": [
        { "ingredientId": {{ingredientId1}}, "quantity": 1 },
        { "ingredientId": {{ingredientId2}}, "quantity": 1 }
    ],
    "scheduledFor": "2026-04-23T10:00:00+05:30",
    "deliveryTimeSlot": "10:00 AM"
}

###


